wireguard-mc
============

This package provides a customized wireguard-go that speaks WireGuard over
TCP with optional Minecraft protocol camouflage. Both tunnel ends must use
this binary (not kernel WireGuard / stock UDP wireguard-go).

The package only ships two local config examples:

  /etc/wireguard/wireguard-go-master.json.example   Master (control plane)
  /etc/wireguard/wireguard-go-agent.json.example    Agent (tunnel node)

Everything else - VPN addresses, links, routes, port forwards, transport /
MC camouflage settings - is managed in the Master web UI and pushed to
agents over the control connection.

Master
------

A host installed as master cannot also run an agent tunnel.

1. sudo wireguard-go install master
   (creates /etc/wireguard/wireguard-go-master.json from the example)
2. Edit /etc/wireguard/wireguard-go-master.json:
     listen, adminPassword, dataDir
3. sudo systemctl restart wireguard-go-master
4. Open http://HOST:8443/ and log in with adminPassword
5. The enroll key (a random one is generated on first start) and the
   address pool for new nodes are shown and edited in the web UI.

Agent
-----

1. sudo wireguard-go install
   (creates /etc/wireguard/wireguard-go-agent.json from the example)
2. Edit /etc/wireguard/wireguard-go-agent.json:
     {
       "masterUrl": "http://MASTER:8443",
       "key": "<enroll key from the Master web UI>"
     }
   After the first enroll the key is replaced with the node token.
3. sudo systemctl restart wireguard-go@wg0

Upgrade
-------

  sudo wireguard-go update          # check GitHub Releases and upgrade
  sudo wireguard-go update --check  # only report

apt / dpkg upgrades restart running wireguard-go@* instances and the Master.

Service management
------------------

  systemctl status wireguard-go@wg0        journalctl -u wireguard-go@wg0 -f
  systemctl status wireguard-go-master     journalctl -u wireguard-go-master -f

  sudo wireguard-go uninstall [--purge]            # agent
  sudo wireguard-go uninstall master [--purge]     # master

install / uninstall / update auto-elevate when not root (sudo -n, pkexec,
then interactive sudo).

Foreground (debug):

  sudo LOG_LEVEL=verbose /usr/bin/wireguard-go -f wg0
  sudo /usr/bin/wireguard-go master

Paths
-----

  Binary:  /usr/bin/wireguard-go
  Config:  /etc/wireguard/
  Data:    /var/lib/wireguard-mc/  (Master SQLite mesh.db)
  Units:   /lib/systemd/system/wireguard-go@.service
           /lib/systemd/system/wireguard-go-master.service
